id: slot-symlink-misdirected-593
category: slot-symlink
images: rs-oracle9
targets: rhel9
key: kernel.randomize_va_space
xfail_issue:
comment: #593 FIXED (RuleSteward session 9m lane 2): 99-sysctl.conf is a symlink pointing NOT at ../sysctl.conf but at another real file (../rs9k1-hidden.conf, outside the sysctl.d search dirs so it is never independently enumerated). The REAL oracle follows the symlink and applies kernel.randomize_va_space=2 (COMPLIANT). RuleSteward's enumerate() now gates the 99-slot content-skip on slot_symlink_ok(), so a symlink at the 99 slot that does not resolve to etc/sysctl.conf is followed and parsed like any ordinary drop-in - RuleSteward now agrees the key is 2 (compliant under both STIG and CIS) and emits no sysctld-W02/W04 finding for it, matching the real oracle's verdict. See the scenario's own special-case arm in sysctld_corpus_oracle.rs for why this is asserted as an absence rather than a value comparison.
